# Editor and agent tooling config. Not written by hand — but `prettier --check .`
# walks it anyway, so an unformatted file generated by somebody's editor or by a
# tool installer fails `npm run verify` on a file that has nothing to do with the
# project. Found by running the gate in a clean checkout.
#
# `.claude/` is no longer entirely untracked: `.claude/settings.json` and
# `.claude/skills/graphify/` are committed (DEC-008). They are vendor- and
# tool-generated all the same, and are not ours to reformat.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.serena/

# Graphify's generated graph, report and AST cache. Gitignored (DEC-008), but
# prettier walks the working tree, not the index — without this line a freshly
# built graph fails `npm run format:check` on ~50 files of machine output.
graphify-out/

# Video output: the rendered cuts, their Hyperframes projects, the extracted
# audio data and the plans written beside them. Same reasoning as graphify-out/
